# Cloudflare Pages header rules (see HARDWARE_TESTING.md §5).
#
# The app is a small static site (Cloudflare Pages caps a single file at 25 MiB).
# The WASM runtime ships in the site (CPU-only bundle, under the cap); the model
# is NOT served from here — it lives on Hugging Face and the service worker
# (public/sw.js) proxies it through as a same-origin response. The rules below
# therefore cover only the app shell.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# The app shell is tiny and its markup carries the build stamp, so serves must
# revalidate every time: `no-cache` still permits reusing a 304'd body, which is
# how a browser ends up showing an old harness after an edit.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store

# The service worker itself must never be cached, or clients get stuck on an
# old cache version.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The worker script is content-addressed by deploy; revalidate so an update is
# picked up without waiting out a long TTL.
/inference-worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
